<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05CU">Example <span data-tag="05CU">4.8.7.5</span>.</a> When $n = 0$, Theorem <a data-tag="05CS" href="/tag/05CS">4.8.7.3</a> asserts that every functor of $\infty $-categories $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ admits a factorization $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\xrightarrow {F'} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}' \xrightarrow {G} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, where the functor $G$ is fully faithful and the functor $F'$ is essentially surjective. For example, we can take $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}' \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ to be the essential image of the functor $F$ (Definition <a data-tag="06S2" href="/tag/06S2">4.8.1.11</a>), and $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}' \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ to be the inclusion map. See Remark <a data-tag="01JR" href="/tag/01JR">4.8.1.12</a>. </p>
